t(\"Confusion Matrix:\")\n    print(confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred))\n    print()\n```\n\nThis code performs the following tasks:\n\n1.  Loads the iris dataset and converts it into a pandas DataFrame.\n2.  Displays statistical summaries of the data using the `describe` method.\n3.  Visualizes the distribution of the data using histograms.\n4.  Displays the distribution of the target variable using a bar chart.\n5.  Splits the data into training and testing sets using the `train_test_split` function.\n6.  Scales the data using the `StandardScaler` from scikit-learn.\n7.  Applies PCA for dimensionality reduction.\n8.  Trains three machine learning models (Random Forest Classifier, Logistic Regression, and Support Vector Machine) on the scaled and reduced data.\n9.  Evaluates the performance of each model using accuracy score, classification report, and confusion matrix."
