"```python\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\nfrom airflow import DAG\nfrom airflow.operators.bash_operator import BashOperator\nfrom airflow.operators.python_operator import PythonOperator\nfrom airflow.providers.celery.operators.celery import CeleryTask\n\ndefault_args = {\n    'owner': 'airflow',\n    'depends_on_past': False,\n    'start_date': datetime(2023, 3, 21),\n    'retries': 1,\n    'retry_delay': timedelta(minutes=5),\n}\n\ndag = DAG(\n    'data_pipeline_dag',\n    default_args=default_args,\n    schedule_interval=timedelta(days=1),\n)\n\ndef create_data_pipeline(**kwargs):\n    # Define tasks here\n    task1 = BashOperator(\n        task_id='task1',\n        bash_command='echo \"Task 1\" > output.txt',\n        dag=dag\n    )\n    task2 = BashOperator(\n        task_id='task2',\n        bash_command='echo \"Task 2\" >> output.txt',\n        dag=dag\n    )\n    task3 = PythonOperator(\n        task_id='task3',\n        python_callable=create_data,\n        dag=dag\n    )\n    return task1, task2, task3\n\ncreate_data = lambda: print(\"Creating data...\")\n\ntask1, task2, task3 = create_data_pipeline()\n\n# Define dependencies\ntask1 >> task2\ntask2 >> task3\n```"
"```python\nimport daemon\nimport logging\nimport os\nimport signal\nimport sys\n\n# Set up logging\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\n\ndef main():\n    # Create a new daemon process\n    with daemon.DaemonContext():\n        # Set up logging in the daemon process\n        logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\n        \n        # Run the main function\n        run()\n\ndef run():\n    # Main function\n    while True:\n        # Your main function logic here\n        logging.info(\"Daemon process running...\")\n        sys.exit(0)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nThis code creates a daemon process using the `daemon` module. The `DaemonContext` class is used to create a new daemon process. The logging setup is also done within the daemon context to ensure that logs are written to the daemon's log file.\n\nIn the `run` function, you can put your main function logic here. The daemon process will continue to run until it is manually stopped or the program is terminated.\n\nTo use this code, save it to a file (e.g., `daemon.py`) and run it with `python daemon.py`. The daemon process will be created and will continue to run until it is stopped.\n\nNote: The `daemon` module is not included in Python's standard library, so you may need to install it separately using pip: `pip install python-daemon`"
"```python\ndef ascii_table(data):\n    # Find the maximum length of strings in the data\n    max_length = max(len(str(item)) for item in data)\n\n    # Print the header row\n    print(\"{:<{width}} | \".format(\"Key\", max_length), end=\"\")\n    for i in range(max_length):\n        print(\"---\", end=\" \")\n    print()\n\n    # Print each row of the table\n    for item in data:\n        print(\"{:<{width}} | \".format(str(item), max_length), end=\"\")\n        for i in range(max_length):\n            print(\" \", end=\" \")\n        print()\n\n# Example usage:\ndata = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\nascii_table(data)\n```"
"```python\nimport re\n\nclass UserAgentParser:\n    def __init__(self, user_agent):\n        self.user_agent = user_agent\n\n    def parse(self):\n        # Match major browser types\n        browser_types = {\n            r'MSIE|Trident': 'Internet Explorer',\n            r'MSIE\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Internet Explorer',\n            r'Opera\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Opera',\n            r'Mobile\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Mobile Browser',\n            r'Android\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Android',\n            r'IEMobile\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Internet Explorer Mobile',\n            r'WPDesktop\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Windows Phone',\n            r'WPMobile\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Windows Phone',\n            r'Fennec': 'Fennec (Firefox for Android)',\n            r'Mobile\\s+Fennec': 'Fennec (Firefox for Android)',\n            r'Android\\s+Fennec': 'Fennec (Firefox for Android)',\n            r'Firefox\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Firefox',\n            r'Firefox\\s+([0-9.]+)\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Firefox',\n            r'Safari\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Safari',\n            r'Chrome\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Chrome',\n            r'Edge\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Edge',\n            r'Edge\\s+([0-9.]+)\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Edge',\n            r'Chrome\\s+([0-9.]+)\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Chrome',\n            r'IEMobile\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Internet Explorer Mobile',\n            r'Windows\\s+Phone\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Windows Phone',\n            r'WPDesktop\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Windows Phone',\n            r'Android\\s+([0-9.]+)': 'Android'\n        }\n\n        # Match browser versions\n        version_pattern = r'(?:([0-9.]+)\\s*)'\n        for browser, pattern in browser_types.items():\n            match = re.search(pattern, self.user_agent, re.IGNORECASE)\n            if match:\n                return f\"{browser} {match.group(1) or 'Unknown'}\"\n\n        # Default to 'Unknown'\n        return 'Unknown'\n\n# Example usage\nuser_agent = \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/74.0.3729.169 Safari/537.3\"\nparser = UserAgentParser(user_agent)\nprint(parser.parse())  # Output: Chrome 74.0.3729.169\n```"
"```python\nfrom confluent import KafkaClient\nfrom confluent import Producer\n\n# Create a new Kafka client\nclient = KafkaClient({'bootstrap.servers': ['localhost:9092']})\n\n# Create a new producer\nproducer = client.create_producer()\n\n# Send a message to a Kafka topic\nmessage = {'hello': 'world'}\nfuture = producer.send('my-topic', message)\n\n# Wait for the message to be sent\nfuture.result(timeout=10)\n\n# Flush any remaining messages in the producer buffer\nproducer.flush()\n```"
"```python\nimport avro.io\nimport avro.schema\nimport socket\n\n# Create a schema for the data structure\nschema = avro.schema.Parse(\n    b\"\"\"\n    {\n      \"type\": \"record\",\n      \"name\": \"Person\",\n      \"fields\": [\n        {\"name\": \"name\", \"type\": \"string\"},\n        {\"name\": \"age\", \"type\": \"int\"}\n      ]\n    }\n    \"\"\",\n    avro.io.Utf8Decoder()\n)\n\n# Create a person instance\nperson = {\n    \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n    \"age\": 30\n}\n\n# Serialize the person instance into a byte string using the schema\nbinary = avro.io.DatumWriter(schema).write(person)\n\n# Create a socket connection to the server\nserver_socket = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\nserver_socket.connect((\"localhost\", 12345))\n\n# Send the serialized byte string over the network connection\nserver_socket.sendall(binary)\n\n# Close the socket connection\nserver_socket.close()\n```"
"```python\nimport click\n\n@click.group()\ndef cli():\n    \"\"\"A simple command-line interface using Click.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n@cli.command()\n@click.option('--name', prompt='Your name', help='The name to greet.')\ndef hello(name):\n    \"\"\"Greet the user by name.\"\"\"\n    click.echo(f'Hello, {name}!')\n\n@cli.command()\n@click.option('--name', prompt='Your name', help='The name to greet.')\n@click.option('--message', default='How are you?', help='The message to send.')\ndef greet(name, message):\n    \"\"\"Greet the user by name and send a message.\"\"\"\n    click.echo(f'{message}, {name}!')\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    cli()\n```"
"```python\nimport json\nimport os\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport yaml\n\nclass PreCommitHookManager:\n    def __init__(self, config_file='config.yaml'):\n        self.config_file = config_file\n        self.config = self.load_config()\n        self.hooks = {}\n\n    def load_config(self):\n        if not os.path.exists(self.config_file):\n            with open(self.config_file, 'w') as f:\n                json.dump({}, f)\n        with open(self.config_file, 'r') as f:\n            return json.load(f)\n\n    def add_hook(self, language, hook_script):\n        self.hooks[language] = hook_script\n        self.save_config()\n\n    def remove_hook(self, language):\n        if language in self.hooks:\n            del self.hooks[language]\n        self.save_config()\n\n    def run_hooks(self, vcs, commit_message):\n        hooks_to_run = [hook for language, hook in self.hooks.items() if vcs == 'git' or vcs == 'svn']\n        for hook in hooks_to_run:\n            if 'shell' in hook:\n                self.run_shell_hook(hook['shell'], commit_message)\n            elif 'python' in hook:\n                self.run_python_hook(hook['python'], commit_message)\n\n    def run_shell_hook(self, hook_script, commit_message):\n        hook_path = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), hook_script)\n        if os.path.exists(hook_path):\n            subprocess.check_call([hook_path], args=(commit_message,))\n        else:\n            print(f\"Hook script {hook_path} does not exist.\")\n\n    def run_python_hook(self, hook_script, commit_message):\n        hook_path = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), hook_script)\n        if os.path.exists(hook_path):\n            subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, hook_path], args=(commit_message,))\n        else:\n            print(f\"Hook script {hook_path} does not exist.\")\n\n    def save_config(self):\n        with open(self.config_file, 'w') as f:\n            json.dump(self.hooks, f)\n\n# Usage\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    manager = PreCommitHookManager()\n    manager.add_hook('python', {'shell': 'pre-commit.sh'})\n    manager.add_hook('java', {'python': 'pre-commit_java.py'})\n    manager.run_hooks('git', 'Commit message')\n```\n\nThis code creates a class `PreCommitHookManager` that manages pre-commit hooks for multiple languages and version control systems. It loads a configuration file `config.yaml` that defines the hooks and their associated languages. The `run_hooks` method runs the hooks during the commit process, and the `add_hook` and `remove_hook` methods allow you to add and remove hooks from the configuration file. The `run_shell_hook` and `run_python_hook` methods run the hooks as shell scripts or Python scripts, respectively."
"```python\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, ValidationError\nimport json\n\n# Define the configuration schema\nclass Config(BaseModel):\n    database_url: str = \"\"\n    database_name: str = \"\"\n    database_user: str = \"\"\n    database_password: str = \"\"\n\n    # Define validation rules\n    @root_validator(pre=True)\n    def validate_database_url(cls, values):\n        if not values['database_url'].startswith('sqlite://'):\n            raise ValueError(\"Database URL must be a valid SQLite connection string\")\n        return values\n\n    @root_validator(pre=True)\n    def validate_database_name(cls, values):\n        if not values['database_name'].isalnum():\n            raise ValueError(\"Database name must be alphanumeric\")\n        return values\n\n# Load the configuration file\nwith open('config.json', 'r') as f:\n    config_data = json.load(f)\n\ntry:\n    # Attempt to validate the configuration\n    config = Config(**config_data)\nexcept ValidationError as e:\n    # Print the error messages\n    for error in e.errors():\n        print(f\"Error: {error['loc'][0]} - {error['msg']}\")\nelse:\n    # Print the validated configuration\n    print(\"Validated Configuration:\")\n    print(config)\n```"
