"```python\nfrom ua_parser import user_agent_parser\n\ndef parse_user_agent(user_agent_string):\n    parsed_data = user_agent_parser.parse(user_agent_string)\n    return parsed_data\n\ndef identify_device(user_agent_string):\n    parsed_data = parse_user_agent(user_agent_string)\n    device_type = parsed_data.get('device')\n    browser_type = parsed_data.get('browser')\n    browser_version = parsed_data.get('browser_version')\n    device_type = 'Phone' if device_type == 'mobile' else 'Tablet'\n    return {\n        'device_type': device_type,\n        'browser_type': browser_type,\n        'browser_version': browser_version\n    }\n\n# Example usage:\nuser_agent_string = \"Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 14_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/14.2 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1\"\ndevice_info = identify_device(user_agent_string)\nprint(device_info)\n```\n\nThis code uses the `ua-parser` library to parse the user agent string and identify the device type (phone or tablet), browser type, and browser version."
